Package: illumex
Type: Package
Title: A Data Interrogation Engine for Enabling Inference
Version: 0.0.8.9004
Authors@R: person(given = "Craig", family = "Hutton",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "craig.hutton@gmail.com")
Description: The exploratory half of the 'illume' workflow, usable on its
    own. It describes every column of a data frame in one call, with a
    Gaussian index in place of a normality test; counts values, finds
    duplicated and copied rows, and reports problems that belong to pairs of
    columns; cleans and recodes; gives bootstrap intervals for a statistic or
    a difference between groups without a model; flags values extreme for
    their own column and rows implausible as a combination, by low-rank
    reconstruction with a simulated null or by isolation forest; describes
    missing values and plots their pattern; and profiles a dataset by
    dimension reduction, generalised low rank models and clustering, for
    numeric and mixed columns alike. Plots are built on 'tinyplot' and named
    for what they show, and the grouped arithmetic runs on 'collapse'.
    Every function is prefixed ilm_, as in 'illume', which attaches this
    package.
